/* The operator console. The product's warm-editorial palette, at a denser rhythm: this is
   a page somebody scans for a number, not one they read.

   Typography is the system UI stack on purpose. The site vendors its fonts because its
   typography is part of what readers are shown and what the owner approves; an internal
   console carries no such promise, and looking native is the better default for one. */

:root {
  --paper: #f6f3ec;
  --card: #fdfcf8;
  --ink: #201e19;
  --muted: #6e685c;
  --rule: #e2dccc;

  /* Magnitude has one job and one hue: bar length carries the number, so colour does not
     have to. */
  --mark: #a8382a;

  /* Reserved for state, never for a series. Every chip carries its word as well, so the
     colour is a second signal and never the only one — which is also what keeps the
